{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require level 4 teaching diploma & DBS checks for all music instrument teachers",
        "additional_details": "We believe requiring an Ofqual Level 4 diploma as the benchmark for instrumental music teaching professionalises the sector by embedding evidence-based pedagogy, technical rigor, and standard accountability. Crucially, coupling this with mandatory safeguarding training helps protect children and vulnerable adults within vulnerable 1-to-1 learning environments. Tutors learn to enforce professional boundaries, and prevent physical or auditory injuries. Mandatory standards can elevate teaching quality.",
        "background": "Reform the Music Education Framework to protect children and vulnerable adults from this existing unregulated sector of education by requiring every music instrument teacher to be qualified in teaching to a minimum level 4 diploma and have a DBS check.",
